  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia ratified the following ILO Conventions -the Migration for Employment Convention (Revised), 1949 (No.97), the Migrant Workers (Supplementary Provisions) Convention, 1975 (No. 143), and the Private Employment Agencies Convention, 1997 (No. 181) which were registered on 8 March 2021. 

In addition, the ratification of three ILO Conventions Nos.  155, 187 and 190 was registered with the ILO on 8 March 2021.  This is equally important to promote the rights of migrant workers in the country.
 With the support of the European Union, the ILO provided technical support to the tripartite constituents in Somalia through a series of awareness raising and sensitization campaigns at the national and regional level to facilitate the ratification and implementation of key ILO Conventions. To this end, the ILO facilitated/supported the tripartite constituents organize 4 advocacy missions to regional states, organize 6 workshops to engage with the regional and federal parliamentarians, conduct a series of public awareness raising campaigns on print, TV, Radio and Social media as well as in the production of various information and education materials.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1.2. Number of ratifications of up-to-date technical Conventions, including those recommended by the Governing Body in the context of the Standards Review Mechanism</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Tripartite Consultation (International Labour Standards) Convention, 1976 (No. 144) was ratified, and registered with the ILO on 8 March 2021. With the support of the European Union, the ILO provided technical support to the tripartite constituents in Somalia through a series of awareness raising and sensitization campaigns at the national and regional level to facilitate ratification and implementation of key ILO Conventions. To this end, the ILO facilitated/supported the tripartite constituents to organize 4 advocacy missions to regional states, organize 6 workshops to engage with the regional and federal parliamentarians, conduct a series of public awareness raising campaigns in print, TV, Radio and Social media as well as in the production of various information and education materials.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1.1. Number of ratifications of fundamental and governance Conventions or Protocols</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
